{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1524450-homebrew-ectophagia-rework","id":1524450,"title":"[Homebrew] Ectophagia Rework","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-23T18:19:17-07:00","id":1524450,"title":"[Homebrew] Ectophagia Rework","content":"This is a rework of how Ectophagia functions! I've heard a lot of people complain about how punishing it is, and I wanted to revise it. Feedback is welcome!<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <u><b>Sin-Eater Ectophagia</b></u><br /> <br /> Committing ectophagia is a Universal trigger for all Geists. Even though Geists cannot harm their Bound, they will attempt to stop the Bound from doing the act unless the Bound uses Intercession. Completely consuming a ghost/Geist with ectophagia causes an automatic loss of one point of Synergy.<br /> <br /> Ectophagia on a ghost (Rank 2 or below) is the process of slowly devouring the Corpus of a helpless ghost. It deals 1 aggravated damage a turn, converting each point of Corpus devoured into a point of Plasm. Ghosts with aggravated damage in their rightmost Corpus box from this process are utterly destroyed and do not reform, even if they have Essence remaining. Upon finishing their meal, the Sin-Eater gets additional Plasm equal to their victim\u2019s Size <i>(as per Destruction on page 195)</i>.<br /> <br /> Ectophagia on a Geist (Rank 3 or above) follows the same process as above, except for when the Bound finishes their meal. The Bound instead fully replenishes their Plasm pool and gains the Geist\u2019s innate Key. A Geist destroyed in this manner does not leave behind a Deathmask Memento.<br /> <br /> Ectophagia on a Castoff simply grants Plasm equal to its Size.<br /> <br /> Tyrants do not have to worry about Crisis Points or Tyranny Loss for committing ectophagia.<br /> <br /> <i>Reminder: Committing ectophagia on a Castoff or Barghest is not a breaking point (or a crisis point / Synergy loss for the Bound).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Ghost Ectophagia</b></u><br /> <br /> There are two forms of stealing Essence for ghosts: Essence Theft and Ectophagia.<br /> <br /> <i>Essence Theft:</i> Ghosts can attempt to steal Essence from one another. The attacking ghost rolls Power + Finesse, contested by the victim\u2019s Power + Resistance. If the attacker succeeds, it steals up to the successes in Essence, as long as the victim has Essence remaining to lose.<br /> <br /> <i>Ectophagia:</i> Direct consumption follows rules similar to Bound, where the target must be incapable of fighting back. This process deals 1 aggravated damage a turn, stealing 1 Essence per damage dealt. Upon finishing their meal, they steal whatever remaining Essence the victim had, utterly destroying them. Even attempting this process is a breaking point for all ghosts.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T06:57:59-07:00","id":1524474,"title":"","content":"(aside, a rank 3-5 ghost isn't necessarily a geist, there are at least two ways discussed in the book where ghosts can increase rank but only drinking from one of the rivers of the Underworld does one become a geist).<br /> <br /> What about other entities, like kerboroi or cthonic beings? And are Barghest treated like normal ghosts (apart from not upsetting the geist)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T16:48:13-07:00","id":1524488,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Good luck eating a Kerberoi. If you manage to, I guess treat it like a normal ghosts since they don't have Keys?</li> <li>Chthonians are nigh-impossible to eat, as &quot;Ghosts who commit ectophagia on Chthonians suffer 1 lethal wound per Essence they would gain, and gain no Essence.&quot; (pg 198) Aka, with these rules, dealing 1 aggravated by eating a Chthonian would cause you to gain no Plasm and take 1 lethal.</li> <li>Barghests are like normal ghosts when it comes to being consumed.</li> </ol>Something I didn't consider is Geist Barghests (a Barghest who drank from the Rivers), in which case I'd say they've evolved beyond being a simple animal ghost and the Geist connected to a Bound committing ectophagia on the Geist Barghest would act like it's a crisis point and Synergy loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}